# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "On a real quantum processor, noise turns the pure state $|\\psi\\rangle$ that a circuit is designed to prepare into a mixed state $\\rho$. Full quantum state tomography can reconstruct $\\rho$, but the number of measurements it needs grows exponentially with the number of qubits. Votto et al. [\\[1\\]](#references) instead learned a compact model of $\\rho$ for up to 96 qubits from randomized measurements. This tutorial follows their workflow.\n"
msgstr "Sa isang totoong quantum processor, ginagawa ng ingay na mixed state na $\\rho$ ang pure state na $|\\psi\\rangle$ na dinisenyong ihanda ng isang circuit. Kayang buuin muli ng buong quantum state tomography ang $\\rho$, pero lumalaki nang exponential ang bilang ng mga measurement na kailangan nito kasabay ng bilang ng mga qubit. Sa halip, natutunan nina Votto et al. [\\[1\\]](#references) ang isang compact na model ng $\\rho$ hanggang 96 qubit mula sa mga randomized measurement. Sinusunod ng tutorial na ito ang workflow nila.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a randomized measurement [\\[2\\]](#references), every qubit $i$ is rotated by an independent random unitary $u_i$ and then measured in the computational basis. One draw of the rotations is called a *measurement setting*, and each setting is repeated for $N_M$ shots. A shot with outcome bits $s_i$ gives the *classical shadow* [\\[3\\]](#references)\n"
msgstr "Sa isang randomized measurement [\\[2\\]](#references), bawat qubit na $i$ ay iniikot ng isang independiyenteng random na unitary na $u_i$ at saka sinusukat sa computational basis. Tinatawag na *measurement setting* ang isang draw ng mga pag-ikot, at inuulit ang bawat setting para sa $N_M$ shot. Ang isang shot na may outcome bit na $s_i$ ay nagbibigay ng *classical shadow* [\\[3\\]](#references)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat\\rho=\\bigotimes_{i=1}^{N}\\left(3\\,u_i^\\dagger|s_i\\rangle\\langle s_i|u_i-\\mathbb{1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\hat\\rho=\\bigotimes_{i=1}^{N}\\left(3\\,u_i^\\dagger|s_i\\rangle\\langle s_i|u_i-\\mathbb{1}\\right),\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "whose average over settings and shots is $\\rho$. The prerequisite tutorial draws each $u_i$ from the three Pauli bases; this tutorial, like the paper, draws them uniformly from all single-qubit unitaries (Haar random), and the same formula applies.\n"
msgstr "na ang average nito sa mga setting at shot ay $\\rho$. Kinukuha ng prerequisite na tutorial ang bawat $u_i$ mula sa tatlong Pauli basis; ang tutorial na ito, tulad ng paper, ay kinukuha ang mga ito nang uniform mula sa lahat ng single-qubit unitary (Haar random), at pareho pa rin ang formula.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shadows estimate properties of a few qubits at a time. The paper combines them into a *matrix product operator* (MPO), which writes the density matrix as a chain of small tensors, one per qubit; noisy states with short-range correlations need only small bonds between neighboring tensors. Like the density matrix renormalization group (DMRG) algorithm, the learner sweeps along the chain and updates one tensor at a time, so that the model matches the shadows on the window of $2\\ell+1$ qubits centered on that tensor (Equation 4 of the paper). The bond dimension stays fixed during these updates, so the learner never truncates the model. Because data enter only through these windows, the number of settings needed does not grow with the length of the chain.\n"
msgstr "Tinatantya ng mga shadow ang mga katangian ng ilang qubit sa isang pagkakataon. Pinagsasama ng paper ang mga ito sa isang *matrix product operator* (MPO), na isinusulat ang density matrix bilang isang kadena ng maliliit na tensor, isa bawat qubit; ang mga maingay na state na may short-range na correlation ay nangangailangan lang ng maliliit na bond sa pagitan ng magkakalapit na tensor. Tulad ng density matrix renormalization group (DMRG) algorithm, nag-i-sweep ang learner sa kadena at nag-a-update ng isang tensor sa bawat pagkakataon, kaya tumutugma ang model sa mga shadow sa window na $2\\ell+1$ qubit na nakasentro sa tensor na iyon (Equation 4 ng paper). Nananatiling fixed ang bond dimension habang ginagawa ang mga update na ito, kaya hindi kailanman nagta-truncate ng model ang learner. Dahil sa mga window na ito lang pumapasok ang data, hindi lumalaki ang bilang ng mga setting na kailangan kasabay ng haba ng kadena.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The settings are split into a training set and a testing set. On the testing set, the paper estimates the max fidelity between $\\rho$ and the model $\\sigma$,\n"
msgstr "Hinahati ang mga setting sa isang training set at isang testing set. Sa testing set, tinatantya ng paper ang max fidelity sa pagitan ng $\\rho$ at ng model na $\\sigma$,\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}(\\rho,\\sigma)=\\frac{\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)}{\\max\\left(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2,\\ \\mathrm{tr}\\,\\sigma^2\\right)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}(\\rho,\\sigma)=\\frac{\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)}{\\max\\left(\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2,\\ \\mathrm{tr}\\,\\sigma^2\\right)}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ directly would take exponentially many measurements. Instead, the paper assumes the *approximate factorization condition* (AFC): correlations in $\\rho$ decay within a few qubits, so global overlaps and purities factor into terms on blocks of $k$ neighboring qubits. The purity also gives the Rényi-2 entropy $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2$, which measures how mixed the state is.\n"
msgstr "Ang direktang pagsukat sa $\\mathrm{tr}(\\rho\\sigma)$ ay mangangailangan ng exponential na dami ng measurement. Sa halip, ina-assume ng paper ang *approximate factorization condition* (AFC): bumababa ang mga correlation sa $\\rho$ sa loob ng ilang qubit, kaya ang mga global na overlap at purity ay nagfa-factor sa mga term sa mga block ng $k$ magkakalapit na qubit. Ibinibigay rin ng purity ang Rényi-2 entropy na $S_2=-\\log_2\\mathrm{tr}\\,\\rho^2$, na sumusukat kung gaano kahalo ang state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The paper prepares the depth-$D$ kicked-Ising state\n"
msgstr "Inihahanda ng paper ang depth-$D$ na kicked-Ising state\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle=\\left(\\prod_{j} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}\\prod_j e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X_j}\\right)^{D}|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle=\\left(\\prod_{j} e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}\\prod_j e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X_j}\\right)^{D}|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "on 96 qubits of `ibm_brisbane`, an Eagle processor, with 2,048 settings of 1,024 shots for $D=1$. Figure 1(c,d) of the paper reports two results for $D=1$:\n"
msgstr "sa 96 qubit ng `ibm_brisbane`, isang Eagle processor, na may 2,048 setting ng 1,024 shot para sa $D=1$. Dalawang resulta para sa $D=1$ ang iniuulat ng Figure 1(c,d) ng paper:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learned model reaches $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}\\approx 75\\%$ with the experimental state at $N=96$, far above the overlap of the ideal state $|\\psi\\rangle$ with the experiment.\n"
msgstr "Naaabot ng natutunang model ang $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}\\approx 75\\%$ kasama ang experimental na state sa $N=96$, na higit na mataas kaysa sa overlap ng ideal na state na $|\\psi\\rangle$ at ng eksperimento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entropy grows linearly, $S_2\\approx(0.14\\text{ to }0.15)\\,N$, and the entropy of the model agrees with an independent estimate from the testing set.\n"
msgstr "Linear ang paglaki ng entropy, $S_2\\approx(0.14\\text{ hanggang }0.15)\\,N$, at tumutugma ang entropy ng model sa independiyenteng tantiya mula sa testing set.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial checks both results, first in an eight-qubit simulation where the exact answers are known, and then in a new 96-qubit run on `ibm_fez`, a Heron r2 processor. The learner is an independent Julia implementation of the equations in the paper and its supplement.\n"
msgstr "Sinusuri ng tutorial na ito ang parehong resulta, una sa isang eight-qubit na simulation kung saan alam ang mga eksaktong sagot, at saka sa isang bagong 96-qubit na run sa `ibm_fez`, isang Heron r2 processor. Ang learner ay isang independiyenteng Julia implementation ng mga equation sa paper at supplement nito.\n"

