# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The helper module [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), which the Setup cell downloads, implements the learner. The tutorial calls the following functions from it:\n"
msgstr "Ang helper module na [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), na dina-download ng Setup cell, ang nag-iimplement ng learner. Tinatawag ng tutorial ang mga sumusunod na function mula rito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Function | Purpose |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | Exact MPO of the ideal kicked-Ising state, or of the state after local depolarizing noise |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Randomly assign measurement settings to training and testing sets (half each by default) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Shadow estimates of every learning window, from the training settings only |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior for common randomized measurements (CRM), fitted to the measured purity of each window, as in the paper |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Sweep the one-site update of the paper along the chain, starting from the maximally mixed state |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | Exact $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ between two MPOs |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | AFC estimates of $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ from the testing settings, with jackknife error bars |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Function | Layunin |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | Eksaktong MPO ng ideal na kicked-Ising state, o ng state pagkatapos ng local depolarizing noise |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Random na i-assign ang mga measurement setting sa mga training at testing set (kalahati bawat isa bilang default) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Mga shadow estimate ng bawat learning window, mula sa mga training setting lang |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior para sa common randomized measurements (CRM), na naka-fit sa nasukat na purity ng bawat window, gaya ng sa paper |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | I-sweep ang one-site update ng paper sa kahabaan ng kadena, simula sa maximally mixed state |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | Eksaktong $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ at $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ sa pagitan ng dalawang MPO |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | Mga AFC estimate ng $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ at $S_2$ mula sa mga testing setting, na may jackknife na error bar |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learner stores the MPO in the Pauli basis. This keeps the model Hermitian with unit trace, but it does not force the model to be positive semidefinite, so the notebook reports how negative its eigenvalues become.\n"
msgstr "Iniimbak ng learner ang MPO sa Pauli basis. Pinananatili nitong Hermitian na may unit trace ang model, pero hindi nito pinipilit na positive semidefinite ang model, kaya iniuulat ng notebook kung gaano ka-negatibo ang mga eigenvalue nito.\n"

