# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A chain is only as good as its worst qubit, so choose the 96 physical qubits yourself. The `transpile` function of `Qiskit.jl` cannot yet accept a fixed initial layout, and in a test on `ibm_phoenix`, the layout it chose included a qubit with 51% readout error. The following chain is the 96-qubit path in the `ibm_fez` coupling map that the error-aware layout of the Python Qiskit `transpile` function (with `optimization_level=3`) selected from the calibration data of 27 September 2026. Its mean readout error is 1.6%, but a heavy-hex lattice has few 96-qubit paths, and this one includes qubit 35, which has a 15% readout error. Calibrations change, so choose a new chain from the current [calibration data](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) before you run on another day or QPU.\n"
msgstr "Ang isang chain ay kasing-husay lang ng pinakamasamang qubit nito, kaya ikaw mismo ang pumili ng 96 na pisikal na qubit. Hindi pa tumatanggap ng fixed initial layout ang function na `transpile` ng `Qiskit.jl`, at sa isang test sa `ibm_phoenix`, may kasamang qubit na may 51% readout error ang layout na pinili nito. Ang sumusunod na chain ay ang 96-qubit na path sa coupling map ng `ibm_fez` na pinili ng error-aware na layout ng function na `transpile` ng Python Qiskit (na may `optimization_level=3`) mula sa calibration data noong 27 Setyembre 2026. Ang mean na readout error nito ay 1.6%, ngunit kakaunti ang 96-qubit na path sa isang heavy-hex lattice, at kasama sa isang ito ang qubit 35, na may 15% na readout error. Nagbabago ang mga calibration, kaya pumili ng bagong chain mula sa kasalukuyang [calibration data](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) bago ka mag-run sa ibang araw o ibang QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To keep this chain, write the circuits directly in native gates instead of transpiling them. A $U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda)$ gate equals $R_Z(\\phi+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\theta+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\lambda)$ up to a global phase. This decomposition covers both the random rotations and the kick $e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X}=U(\\pi/4,-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$. The gate $e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}$ equals a CZ gate followed by $S^\\dagger$ on both qubits, up to a global phase. Because these $S^\\dagger$ gates are diagonal, they commute with the CZ gates, so each qubit collects one $R_Z(-\\pi/2)$ per bond before its measurement rotation.\n"
msgstr "Para mapanatili ang chain na ito, isulat nang direkta ang mga circuit gamit ang mga native gate sa halip na i-transpile ang mga ito. Ang isang $U(\\theta,\\phi,\\lambda)$ gate ay katumbas ng $R_Z(\\phi+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\theta+\\pi)\\,\\sqrt{X}\\,R_Z(\\lambda)$ hanggang sa isang global phase. Sinasaklaw ng decomposition na ito ang parehong random rotation at ang kick na $e^{-i\\frac{\\pi}{8}X}=U(\\pi/4,-\\pi/2,\\pi/2)$. Ang gate na $e^{i\\frac{\\pi}{4}Z_jZ_{j+1}}$ ay katumbas ng isang CZ gate na sinusundan ng $S^\\dagger$ sa dalawang qubit, hanggang sa isang global phase. Dahil diagonal ang mga $S^\\dagger$ gate na ito, nagko-commute sila sa mga CZ gate, kaya bawat qubit ay nakakaipon ng isang $R_Z(-\\pi/2)$ kada bond bago ang measurement rotation nito.\n"

