# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The model describes the data far better than the ideal state.** At $N=96$, the held-out $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ of the $\\ell=2$ model is 0.59 ± 0.10, compared with 0.0035 for the ideal state. The paper reports about 0.75 on `ibm_brisbane`.\n"
msgstr "**Mas mahusay na inilalarawan ng model ang data kaysa sa ideal na state.** Sa $N=96$, ang held-out na $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ ng $\\ell=2$ na model ay 0.59 ± 0.10, kumpara sa 0.0035 para sa ideal na state. Nag-uulat ang paper ng humigit-kumulang 0.75 sa `ibm_brisbane`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**The entropy of the model agrees with the testing data at every $N$.** At $N=96$, it is 10.2 from the model and 10.0 ± 0.3 from the testing data, or $S_2/N\\approx 0.10$, compared with 0.14 to 0.15 on the older `ibm_brisbane`.\n"
msgstr "**Tugma ang entropy ng model sa testing data sa bawat $N$.** Sa $N=96$, ito ay 10.2 mula sa model at 10.0 ± 0.3 mula sa testing data, o $S_2/N\\approx 0.10$, kumpara sa 0.14 hanggang 0.15 sa mas lumang `ibm_brisbane`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The comparison of window sizes shows where the information is. With $\\ell=1$, the model is almost as good ($\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}=0.55\\pm0.09$), so for these data, correlations beyond a few qubits add little. With $\\ell=0$, the product state misses the entanglement between neighboring qubits: its entropy grows to 32 instead of 10, and its $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ falls even faster than that of the ideal state, to $6\\times10^{-6}$ at $N=96$.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng paghahambing ng mga laki ng window kung nasaan ang impormasyon. Sa $\\ell=1$, halos kasing-husay ang model ($\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}=0.55\\pm0.09$), kaya para sa data na ito, kaunti lang ang naidaragdag ng mga correlation na lampas sa ilang qubit. Sa $\\ell=0$, hindi nakukuha ng product state ang entanglement sa pagitan ng magkakalapit na qubit: lumalaki ang entropy nito hanggang 32 sa halip na 10, at mas mabilis pang bumabagsak ang $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ nito kaysa sa ideal na state, hanggang $6\\times10^{-6}$ sa $N=96$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep the following limitations in mind when you read these numbers:\n"
msgstr "Tandaan ang mga sumusunod na limitasyon kapag binabasa ang mga numerong ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Training split.** The error bars cover the statistical error of the testing data only. Other random splits of the same settings give $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ between 0.49 and 0.59 at $N=96$ for $\\ell=2$.\n"
msgstr "**Training split.** Sinasaklaw lamang ng mga error bar ang statistical error ng testing data. Ang ibang random na split ng parehong mga setting ay nagbibigay ng $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ sa pagitan ng 0.49 at 0.59 sa $N=96$ para sa $\\ell=2$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Final sweep.** The learner always returns the model from the final sweep, so the testing data never influence the model.\n"
msgstr "**Huling sweep.** Laging ibinabalik ng learner ang model mula sa huling sweep, kaya hindi kailanman naiimpluwensyahan ng testing data ang model.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Positivity.** The model is not constrained to be positive semidefinite; its most negative eigenvalue in a learning window is about $-0.05$. Its $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ therefore describe an operator, not certified properties of a physical state.\n"
msgstr "**Positivity.** Ang model ay hindi pinipilit na maging positive semidefinite; ang pinakanegatibong eigenvalue nito sa isang learning window ay humigit-kumulang $-0.05$. Kaya ang $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ at $S_2$ nito ay naglalarawan ng isang operator, hindi ng mga certified na katangian ng isang pisikal na state.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Factorization.** Every held-out estimate relies on the AFC assumption, which the measurements themselves cannot certify.\n"
msgstr "**Factorization.** Ang bawat held-out na pagtatantya ay umaasa sa AFC assumption, na hindi mapapatunayan ng mga sukat mismo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
msgstr "<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga Rekomendasyon\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat the experiment at depth two with the paper's parameters for that depth ($\\ell=3$ and a maximum bond dimension of 8), and determine how many measurement settings the learner needs.\n"
msgstr "Ulitin ang eksperimento sa depth na dalawa gamit ang mga parameter ng paper para sa depth na iyon ($\\ell=3$ at maximum na bond dimension na 8), at alamin kung ilang measurement setting ang kailangan ng learner.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn with the two-site update instead (`update=:two_site` in `training_marginals` and `learn_mpo`), which truncates the bond dimension after every step, and see how it behaves with fewer training settings.\n"
msgstr "Mag-learn gamit ang two-site update sa halip (`update=:two_site` sa `training_marginals` at `learn_mpo`), na nagta-truncate ng bond dimension pagkatapos ng bawat hakbang, at tingnan kung paano ito kumikilos sa mas kaunting training setting.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Learn without the CRM prior (`prior=nothing`) and compare the held-out fidelity.\n"
msgstr "Mag-learn nang walang CRM prior (`prior=nothing`) at ihambing ang held-out na fidelity.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply the same analysis to the authors' published [`ibm_brisbane` measurements](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18323569).\n"
msgstr "Ilapat ang parehong analysis sa mga inilathalang [`ibm_brisbane` na sukat](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18323569) ng mga may-akda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the [supplement of the paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.12550) for the derivation of the update and of the AFC estimators.\n"
msgstr "Basahin ang [supplement ng paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.12550) para sa derivation ng update at ng mga AFC estimator.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Explore other randomized-measurement protocols in the [`RandomMeas.jl` examples](https://github.com/bvermersch/RandomMeas.jl/tree/main/examples).\n"
msgstr "Tuklasin ang iba pang randomized-measurement na protocol sa mga [halimbawa ng `RandomMeas.jl`](https://github.com/bvermersch/RandomMeas.jl/tree/main/examples).\n"

